    <string name="memory_hero_help_title">About memory use</string>
    <string name="memory_hero_help_text">Android keeps recently used apps in memory so they open faster; unused RAM is wasted RAM. \"In use\" is total minus what Android reports as available, which already counts caches it can reclaim instantly. Swap is compressed memory (zram) that holds pages Android moved out of RAM.</string>

    <!-- Honest copy -->
    <string name="memory_honest_title">Android manages memory on its own</string>
    <string name="memory_honest_message">Freeing RAM does not save battery by itself and does not make the phone faster. Stopped apps may restart on their own, and a force-stopped app does not receive notifications or run alarms until you open it again.</string>

    <!-- Without Shizuku -->
    <string name="memory_no_shizuku_title">Running apps need Shizuku</string>
    <string name="memory_no_shizuku_message">Android lets an app see only its own processes. With Shizuku connected, Able can list running apps with their memory and stop the ones you choose. Without it, Android\'s \"Running services\" screen (Developer options) shows the same information.</string>
    <string name="memory_running_services">Running services</string>

    <!-- List -->
    <string name="memory_section_apps">Running apps</string>
    <string name="memory_apps_help_title">About running apps</string>
    <string name="memory_apps_help_text">The list comes from the Android process table (ps) through Shizuku. Memory is resident memory (RSS) summed over the app\'s processes; pages shared with other apps are counted for each of them, so the total can exceed the RAM in use.\n\nForce stop ends every process of the app and keeps it stopped until you or another app opens it: notifications, alarms and background work stop too.\n\nStop background processes asks Android to end only the processes it can safely end; foreground and visible ones keep running.\n\nAble, Shizuku, System UI, the launcher, phone, the current keyboard and persistent system apps are protected and never stopped. Every stop is recorded in the action history.</string>
